      en: "Dakar is the capital of Senegal and is situated on the Cap-Vert Peninsula, the westernmost point of the African mainland. The city was founded in 1857 by the French as a fortified settlement and replaced Saint-Louis as the capital of French West Africa in 1902. This colonial past still shapes the city's appearance today, particularly in the Plateau district with its administrative buildings. Geographically, the city is favored by its strategic location on the Atlantic Ocean, which has made it one of the most important ports in West Africa. Dakar is a significant cultural center, renowned for the IFAN Museum of African Arts and the African Renaissance Monument, the tallest statue in Africa. The nearby Gorée Island, a UNESCO World Heritage site, serves as a memorial to the transatlantic slave trade. Today, the metropolis is a dynamic economic hub with over 1.1 million inhabitants (over 3.7 million in the metropolitan area). It serves as a vital transport hub for sea and air traffic between Europe, the Americas, and the African continent.",
